.TH PGREP 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
pgrep \- list PIDs of processes whose command name matches a pattern
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pgrep
.I pattern
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the PID and command name of every process whose
.B /proc/<pid>/comm
matches
.IR pattern ,
a shell glob (\fB*\fR/\fB?\fR, no character classes) -- the same
matcher
.BR find (1)'s
.B \-name
uses. Matches the short command name, not the full command line with
arguments. Never matches this invocation of \fBpgrep\fR itself.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR, and \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if at least one process matched, 1 if none did, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkill (1),
.BR ps (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR mitos\-box (1)
